module gunbc.repository


data gunbc_repository_authority_note: String = "ONE TYPED ROW FOR THE REPOSITORY THIS PROJECT LIVES IN, because before it there were five spellings and no authority. dag/tools/ci_heal_dispatch carried owner and repo as two bare Strings, dag/gunbc/tools/review and review_codex each carried their own owner/repo pair, dag/gunbc/runner_host_deploy carried org, and dag/gunbc/assimilate/bmc_token_federation carried the slug gunb-ai/gunbc as a third shape again. Five nicknames for one entity is the DESIGN section 3 violation exactly, and it is the kind that stays invisible because every individual literal looks obviously correct.\\n\\nWHY A SIXTH SPELLING WOULD NOT HAVE BEEN ACCEPTABLE, which is the reviewer's point (review 46301) and is correct: an honestly-marked scaffold duplicating a canonical fact is still a violation - DESIGN says so in as many words in its recurring-failure list. The answer to five nicknames is not a sixth carrying a promise to consolidate later; it is one authority the others CONSUME. So this row exists and the five sites now project from it.\\n\\nWHY THE TYPE IS Repository RATHER THAN A PAIR OF STRINGS. extdeps.github.github models what the GitHub API actually returns, so owner, name, full_name, private and default_branch travel together as one fact with one identity. A consumer that needs the default branch stops guessing main, and a consumer that needs the slug stops concatenating one. The bare-String sites could only ever answer the question they were spelled for.\\n\\nWHY IT LIVES IN gunbc RATHER THAN extdeps. The TYPE is an upstream fact and belongs to extdeps; WHICH repository this project is, is a product fact about this project. Putting the instance in extdeps would make the dependency model know about its dependent."

data gunbc_repository: Repository = Repository {
  owner: "gunb-ai",
  name: "gunbc",
  full_name: "gunb-ai/gunbc",
  private: false,
  default_branch: "main",
}
